{"usCongressBioId":"B000049","familyName":"Bailey","givenName":"Theodorus","honorificPrefix":"Mr.","unaccentedFamilyName":"Bailey","unaccentedGivenName":"Theodorus","birthDate":"1758-10-12","birthCirca":false,"birthDateUnknown":false,"deathDate":"1828-01-08","deathCirca":false,"image":[{"contentUrl":"/bioguide-staging/assets/1fa966ae5914a8ec315ae9e23edb7ac6.jpg","caption":"<a href=\"http://www.senate.gov/artandhistory/history/common/generic/Photo_Collection_of_the_Senate_Historical_Office.htm\">Courtesy U.S. Senate Historical Office</a>","name":"B000049_001"}],"profileText":"A Representative and a Senator from New York; born near Fishkill, Dutchess County, N.Y., October 12, 1758; attended the rural schools; studied law; admitted to the bar in 1778 and commenced practice in Poughkeepsie, N.Y.; served in the Revolutionary War, the New York Militia; served in the New York militia, 1786-1805, and attained the rank of brigadier general; elected as Anti-Administration to the Third Congress, and as a Democratic Republican to the Fourth Congresses (March 4, 1793-March 3, 1797); elected as a Democratic Republican to the Sixth Congress (March 4, 1799-March 3, 1801); elected as a Democratic Republican to the Seventh Congress to fill the vacancy caused by the resignation of Thomas Tillotson (October 6, 1801-March 3, 1803); simultaneously served in the New York State assembly in 1802; elected as a Democratic Republican to the United States Senate and served from March 4, 1803, to January 16, 1804, when he resigned to accept the position of postmaster of the city of New York, which he held until his death; died on September 6, 1828, in New York, N.Y.; interment in the Dutch Burying Ground; reinterment in the Rural Cemetery, Poughkeepsie, N.Y., January 8, 1864.","relationship":[],"asset":[{"name":"B000049_001","assetType":"Image","contentUrl":"/bioguide-published/assets/1fa966ae5914a8ec315ae9e23edb7ac6.jpg","creditLine":"<a href=\"http://www.senate.gov/artandhistory/history/common/generic/Photo_Collection_of_the_Senate_Historical_Office.htm\">Courtesy U.S. Senate Historical Office</a>","associatedEntity":[],"usageRight":["Import to Congress.gov"],"uploadDate":"2024-06-21T14:35:25.514","uploadDateISO":"2024-06-21T18:35:25.514Z"}],"jobPositions":[{"job":{"name":"Representative","jobType":"CongressMemberJob"},"startDate":"1793-12-02","startCirca":false,"endCirca":false,"congressAffiliation":{"congress":{"name":"The 3rd United States Congress","congressNumber":3,"congressType":"USCongress","startDate":"1793-03-04","endDate":"1795-03-03"},"partyAffiliation":[{"party":{"name":"Anti-Administration"},"startCirca":false,"endCirca":false}],"represents":{"regionType":"DistrictRegion","regionCode":"NY"}}},{"job":{"name":"Representative","jobType":"CongressMemberJob"},"startDate":"1795-12-07","startCirca":false,"endCirca":false,"congressAffiliation":{"congress":{"name":"The 4th United States Congress","congressNumber":4,"congressType":"USCongress","startDate":"1795-06-08","endDate":"1797-03-03"},"partyAffiliation":[{"party":{"name":"Democratic Republican"},"startCirca":false,"endCirca":false}],"represents":{"regionType":"DistrictRegion","regionCode":"NY"}}},{"job":{"name":"Representative","jobType":"CongressMemberJob"},"startDate":"1799-12-02","startCirca":false,"endCirca":false,"congressAffiliation":{"congress":{"name":"The 6th United States Congress","congressNumber":6,"congressType":"USCongress","startDate":"1799-12-02","endDate":"1801-03-03"},"partyAffiliation":[{"party":{"name":"Democratic Republican"},"startCirca":false,"endCirca":false}],"represents":{"regionType":"StateRegion","regionCode":"NY"}}},{"job":{"name":"Representative","jobType":"CongressMemberJob"},"startDate":"1801-12-07","startCirca":false,"endCirca":false,"congressAffiliation":{"congress":{"name":"The 7th United States Congress","congressNumber":7,"congressType":"USCongress","startDate":"1801-03-04","endDate":"1803-03-03"},"partyAffiliation":[{"party":{"name":"Democratic Republican"},"startCirca":false,"endCirca":false}],"represents":{"regionType":"DistrictRegion","regionCode":"NY"},"note":[{"type":"Note","content":"Elected to fill vacancy caused by the resignation of Thomas Tillotson, and took his sea December 7, 1802.","noteType":"FootNote"}]}},{"job":{"name":"Senator","jobType":"CongressMemberJob"},"startDate":"1803-03-04","startCirca":false,"endDate":"1804-01-16","endCirca":false,"congressAffiliation":{"congress":{"name":"The 8th United States Congress","congressNumber":8,"congressType":"USCongress","startDate":"1803-10-17","endDate":"1805-03-03"},"partyAffiliation":[{"party":{"name":"Democratic Republican"},"startCirca":false,"endCirca":false}],"represents":{"regionType":"StateRegion","regionCode":"NY"}}}],"creativeWork":[],"researchRecord":[{"name":"15 letters (1800-1818) to his brother William Bailey, in the Elizabeth M. Smith collection, 1662-1932. Also a receipt book (1804-1811) primarily recording salary payments to postal employees; includes some personal business. Finding aid.","recordType":["Papers"],"recordLocation":{"name":"New-York Historical Society","location":{"addressLocality":"New York","addressRegion":"NY"}}},{"name":"1 item.","recordType":["Papers"],"recordLocation":{"name":"Boston Public Library","location":{"addressLocality":"Boston","addressRegion":"MA"}}},{"name":"1 letter (January 5, 1812) in the Van Schaack family collection. Finding aid.","recordType":["Papers"],"recordLocation":{"name":"Rare Book and Manuscript Library","location":{"addressLocality":"New York","addressRegion":"NY"},"parentRecordLocation":{"name":"Columbia University","location":{"addressLocality":"New York","addressRegion":"NY"}}}},{"name":"1787-1801. 8 items. 4 letters (May 19, 1787; November 6, 1795; February 26, 1796; June 18, 1796), and 4 receipts. Finding aid.","recordType":["Papers"],"recordLocation":{"name":"Manuscripts and Special Collections","location":{"addressLocality":"Albany","addressRegion":"NY"},"parentRecordLocation":{"name":"New